# Cloudflare Workers static assets are served *before* the Worker runs when a
# path matches a file, so the Worker's own header wrapping never executes for
# these. This file is the only thing that sets headers on them.
#
# Why they matter: the view runs in a frame sandboxed without
# `allow-same-origin`, so its document has an opaque origin and its own
# subresource fetches — CanvasKit, the fonts — arrive as cross-origin requests
# with `Origin: null`. Without these, Flutter never gets a renderer and the
# frame stays blank.

/app/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: cross-origin
